{"title":"Green's Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Green's Theorem</b> is a result in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_analysis\" title=\"Real analysis\">real analysis</a>.  It is\na special case of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stokes%27_Theorem\" title=\"Stokes&#39; Theorem\">Stokes' Theorem</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Green%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a bounded subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00a62d72646c467ae02878bc6dd7138e087a13c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}^2$\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> with positively\noriented boundary <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be functions with\ncontinuous <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partial_derivative\" title=\"Partial derivative\">partial derivatives</a> mapping an open set containing\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />.  Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d61382f7bcb33ab07d9e764ec3c788184718e0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_C \\bigl[ L(x,y)dx + M(x,y)dy \\bigr] = \\iint_D \\left( \\frac{\\partial M} {\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial y} \\right) dA.\\]\" width=\"402\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Green%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It suffices to show that the theorem holds when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is a square,\nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> can always be approximated arbitrarily well with\na finite collection of squares.\n</p><p>Then let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a square with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a53387373f79f3f15a70abeeb58639c7d60aa2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fe40b98e74737c70752abaa29332bc3369bfd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8af9728dcf91aaeddaf4c1e971f7dda90365a8e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d6d6dc851b56cebbf53da871331e0c9674b5bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/e/1ae3ab9d647dcad0f07b6b4fb7a35098ad438914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da395499c40b6f23ec1473c6296931a8d49abd1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\le d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />.  Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/040b5d9e15a5a66e0e005286bb1cdd8089dc6d3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\int_C \\bigl[ L(x,y)dx + M(x,y)dy \\bigr] ={}&amp; \\int_{a}^b L(x,c) dx + \\int_{c}^d M(b,y)dy \\\\ &amp;+ \\int_b^a L(x,d) dx + \\int_{d}^c M(a,y) dy \\\\ ={}&amp; \\int_c^d \\bigl[ M(b,y) - M(a,y) \\bigr] dy + \\int_a^b \\bigl[ L(x,d) - L(x,c) \\bigr] dx . \\end{align*}\" width=\"656\" height=\"143\" />\nNow, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fundamental_Theorem_of_Calculus\" title=\"Fundamental Theorem of Calculus\">Fundamental Theorem of Calculus</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c220a4abfd97459d709a3aedf19d796f80b72ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L(x,d) - L(x,c) = \\int_c^d \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial y}(x) dy\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"44\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa107544a06a0147325a0db85a5c59ac0020df9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M(b,y) - M(a,y) = \\int_a^b \\frac{\\partial M}{\\partial x}(y) dx .\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"44\" />\nHence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e1ba3c617c9d26da07565f44d14c3a4afb923e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\int_c^d \\bigl[ M(b,y) - M(a,y) \\bigr] dx - \\int_a^b \\bigl[ \tL(x,d) - L(x,c) \\bigr] dy &amp;= \\int_c^d \\int_a^b \\frac{\\partial M}{\\partial x} dx dy - \\int_a^b \\int_c^d \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial y} dy dx \\\\ &amp;= \\iint_D \\left( \\frac{\\partial M}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial y} \\right) dA , \\end{align*}\" width=\"709\" height=\"98\" />\nas desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Green%27s_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stokes%27_Theorem\" title=\"Stokes&#39; Theorem\">Stokes' Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divergence_Theorem\" title=\"Divergence Theorem\">Divergence Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy%27s_Integral_Theorem\" title=\"Cauchy&#39;s Integral Theorem\">Cauchy's Integral Theorem</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017102212\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 123/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4518/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8027:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017102212 and revision id 106017. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}